1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:02,961
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,839
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

3
00:00:09,092 --> 00:00:10,468
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

4
00:00:10,552 --> 00:00:12,721
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

5
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ One cut, and it’s over ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,768
- Audrey: What are you doing here?
- Atoy: Oh.

7
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:20,061
Is Georgia with you, huh?

8
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:21,563
Georgia is here?

9
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:22,439
Oh, ah-- why--

10
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:24,524
Why would I be with Georgia? No.

11
00:00:24,607 --> 00:00:26,151
Gavin: I don't eat cookies.

12
00:00:26,234 --> 00:00:27,235
Sorry.

13
00:00:27,318 --> 00:00:27,819
When we were chatting,

14
00:00:27,902 --> 00:00:29,821
you said your favorite is

15
00:00:29,904 --> 00:00:30,989
chocolate chip cookies.

16
00:00:31,072 --> 00:00:32,782
But Rommel, there! That's his favorite!

17
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:34,409
Gavin: Cookies.

18
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:37,579
Chanty: Can we just take a
picture of you holding the cookies?

19
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:39,330
As if you're about to bite it.

20
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:40,206
As a couple.

21
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:41,666
Xavier: Are you here for business?

22
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:42,917
Maybe I can help you out.

23
00:00:43,877 --> 00:00:46,296
No. I don't think that you can help me.

24
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:48,214
Who is Samir talking to?

25
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:49,758
Paldo: Son of a thread.

26
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:50,967
He's The Washer.

27
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:53,094
Doesn't Gavin like me?

28
00:00:53,178 --> 00:00:54,012
Am I ugly?

29
00:00:54,095 --> 00:00:55,513
You never know.

30
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:58,349
Maybe the one who was just introduced
to you will be your forever.

31
00:00:58,433 --> 00:01:01,978
Love, who are you texting?

32
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:04,439
Ah, it's-- Miss Cita.

33
00:01:04,522 --> 00:01:05,648
Ah, hi, brother.

34
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:07,650
[speaking in Russian]
Ok, I will tell The Washer.

35
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:10,403
He speaks Russian?

36
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:13,364
Hey. Are those goons?

37
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:17,869
Tell him he needs to do business on time.

38
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:19,329
Audrey: Why are you wearing shades?

39
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:20,705
Oh, don't they suit me?

40
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:21,331
Emerson: Where's Atoy?

41
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:23,666
He left; he can't come back here anymore.

42
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:25,126
He's already with Audrey.

43
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:26,795
I know who The Washer is.

44
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:29,047
Jesabel: She only looks like
a somewhat well-off mother.

45
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:31,216
But I'm sure she's The Washer,

46
00:01:31,299 --> 00:01:32,967
because she washed her hands!

47
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:35,470
I don't believe they
only came here for a vacation.

48
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:38,932
Make sure they don't notice

49
00:01:39,015 --> 00:01:40,475
that you're investigating them.

50
00:01:40,558 --> 00:01:41,768
Elias: Because you're a police officer.

51
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:42,519
Am I right?

52
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:44,562
Audrey: Let's go, let's go.

53
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:45,897
Wait, sit down first.

54
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,148
Ah-- Ah, let's order again, like, ah…

55
00:01:47,232 --> 00:01:50,401
Atoy: It seems like this-- is not enough.

56
00:01:50,485 --> 00:01:52,278
[music swells]

57
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:53,905
(♪ Fix this ♪)

58
00:01:53,988 --> 00:01:55,323
- Sisig?
- Okay.

59
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:57,283
- Sisig. All right.
- Should we add more?

60
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:58,034
What do you want?

61
00:01:58,118 --> 00:01:58,993
Um…

62
00:02:01,162 --> 00:02:02,580
- Turon?
- Atoy: Turon?

63
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:03,832
It seems too sweet,

64
00:02:03,915 --> 00:02:04,499
never mind, that's okay.

65
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:05,625
The sisig is enough,

66
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:07,544
and your order, and oysters.

67
00:02:07,627 --> 00:02:08,211
Are you sure?

68
00:02:08,294 --> 00:02:09,170
Yeah, that's enough.

69
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:09,879
Just let it be--

70
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:10,588
Let that be.

71
00:02:10,672 --> 00:02:11,256
Okay.

72
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:14,134
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

73
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:17,345
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

74
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,141
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

75
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:23,226
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

76
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:24,602
♪ The hole in my polo

77
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:26,604
that's right under the armpit ♪

78
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:28,064
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

79
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:30,608
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

80
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:33,111
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

81
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:36,781
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

82
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:38,366
[gunshots]

83
00:02:38,449 --> 00:02:40,118
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

84
00:02:40,201 --> 00:02:42,078
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

85
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:44,080
[music swells]

86
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:45,540
(Fix this)

87
00:02:46,082 --> 00:02:47,917
[music fades]

88
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:52,005
[door lock clicks]

89
00:02:53,798 --> 00:02:56,134
[mellow music playing]

90
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:07,353
Love…

91
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:12,525
Can we take this off now?

92
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:14,068
Huh?

93
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:18,615
You think I haven't noticed.

94
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:22,035
You've been restless for a while.

95
00:03:23,202 --> 00:03:25,997
It seems like you're deep in thought.

96
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:28,625
Love, what?

97
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:30,376
Is there a problem?

98
00:03:32,503 --> 00:03:34,297
Why would you think that?

99
00:03:37,091 --> 00:03:38,092
Because it feels like…

100
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:43,806
I'm bothering you by being together.

101
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:45,892
[music continues]

102
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:47,310
Not at all.

103
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:48,937
No-- really not.

104
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:52,815
Ah, I'm sorry because sometimes…

105
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:53,816
[titters]

106
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:57,195
maybe I'm just thinking
about work or something, but…

107
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:02,116
I don't want to be
with anyone else but you.

108
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,826
[sentimental music playing]

109
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:05,536
So…

110
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:09,374
I have you all to myself.

111
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:10,750
[music continues]

112
00:04:10,833 --> 00:04:12,669
Hmm…

113
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:13,253
[smooches]

114
00:04:13,336 --> 00:04:15,004
I'll take a shower first, okay.

115
00:04:15,088 --> 00:04:16,547
I'm so sticky.

116
00:04:16,631 --> 00:04:18,091
[music continues]

117
00:04:20,134 --> 00:04:21,469
Do you want me to join you?

118
00:04:22,136 --> 00:04:24,514
Do you want to join?

119
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:27,058
[music fades]

120
00:04:27,558 --> 00:04:29,143
[soft rock music playing]

121
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:04,095
[knocks on door]

122
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:06,097
Staff: Room service, sir.

123
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:07,974
What a bother, really.

124
00:05:08,057 --> 00:05:10,059
[sneaky music playing]

125
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:11,978
- [door lock clicks]
- Oh, sorry.

126
00:05:12,061 --> 00:05:13,062
Yes?

127
00:05:13,146 --> 00:05:15,648
Staff: Dinner for Mr. and Mrs. Padua?

128
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:17,900
Oh, yeah. That's right.

129
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:19,193
- Do you want-- yeah.
- Staff: I'll just bring it in, sir.

130
00:05:19,277 --> 00:05:19,777
Just put it there.

131
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:20,945
Thank you.

132
00:05:21,029 --> 00:05:23,489
[suspicious music playing]

133
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:33,958
Audrey: Love! Come on!

134
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:37,837
Ah, Audrey, I just need
to get something outside.

135
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:38,504
Okay?

136
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:39,630
Audrey: Love?

137
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:40,465
I just need to get something outside.

138
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:41,215
I'll be back.

139
00:05:41,299 --> 00:05:43,217
[rousing music playing]

140
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:47,555
[door closes]

141
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:49,432
[mysterious music playing]

142
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:56,939
What's in that attaché case?

143
00:05:57,023 --> 00:05:58,858
Why would I tell you?

144
00:05:59,525 --> 00:06:00,735
Give that to me.

145
00:06:00,818 --> 00:06:01,903
Are you serious?

146
00:06:01,986 --> 00:06:02,904
I went through so much for this,

147
00:06:02,987 --> 00:06:03,905
and you'll just take it?

148
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:06,532
Hey! You're Obsidian, right?

149
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:08,284
And you're The Washer.

150
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:10,286
What are you saying?

151
00:06:10,953 --> 00:06:12,205
Give me that!

152
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:13,164
Hey!

153
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:16,542
Hey.

154
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:18,002
[suspicious music playing]

155
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:22,048
Ow, ow.

156
00:06:23,341 --> 00:06:24,675
It hurts.

157
00:06:24,759 --> 00:06:25,843
[music fades]

158
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:32,141
Where did she go?

159
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:33,935
Emerson: Jesabel.

160
00:06:34,685 --> 00:06:36,312
[clicks tongue]

161
00:06:36,395 --> 00:06:36,938
[suspicious music playing]

162
00:06:37,021 --> 00:06:38,606
Where did Jesabel go?

163
00:06:39,607 --> 00:06:40,108
Geez.

164
00:06:40,191 --> 00:06:41,192
Paldo: Hey! Come back here!

165
00:06:41,275 --> 00:06:43,152
Emerson! That's the Washer!

166
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:44,529
- Huh? Really?
- Block him!

167
00:06:44,612 --> 00:06:45,613
- Is that you?
- [thumps]

168
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:46,781
Ow, ow, ow--

169
00:06:46,864 --> 00:06:48,241
Hey! [grunts & groans]

170
00:06:48,324 --> 00:06:49,117
You lunatic.

171
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:49,742
Hey!

172
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:52,120
[grunting & groaning] [thumping]

173
00:06:53,621 --> 00:06:55,665
You, ah. Come here, you!

174
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:57,166
[soft rock music playing]

175
00:06:57,250 --> 00:06:59,210
What's your transaction with Samir, huh?!

176
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:00,920
Who's Samir?

177
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:02,964
- Emerson: What do you mean who's Samir?
- What do you mean who's Sa--

178
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:04,882
Admit it! You're the Washer, aren't you?!

179
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:06,551
Yes, I used to be a dishwasher!

180
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:08,344
But I don't know Samir!

181
00:07:08,427 --> 00:07:10,012
Mmm, huh!

182
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,806
You have the nerve to lie, huh!

183
00:07:12,765 --> 00:07:14,058
You won't admit it, huh!

184
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:15,435
Enough, enough!

185
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:18,271
Yes, I stole that attaché case!

186
00:07:18,354 --> 00:07:20,273
I just stole it from the bald mestizo!

187
00:07:20,356 --> 00:07:21,941
It's full of money!

188
00:07:22,024 --> 00:07:23,693
You stole it?

189
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:24,777
- Well, you're a brazen thief…
- Ow!

190
00:07:24,861 --> 00:07:26,529
… you’re shameless. Hmm?

191
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:27,947
Yes, I'm a thief.

192
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:29,657
I'm a gatecrasher.

193
00:07:30,783 --> 00:07:33,244
Stealing from the rich
has long been my modus!

194
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:34,328
[tense music playing]

195
00:07:34,412 --> 00:07:36,247
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

196
00:07:37,373 --> 00:07:38,332
Maybe-- bro.

197
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:41,335
Maybe he's telling the truth,
maybe he really isn't the Washer.

198
00:07:42,253 --> 00:07:45,381
It seems Jesabel might be
more correct about her prospect.

199
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:48,259
Well, where is Jesabel, anyway?

200
00:07:48,342 --> 00:07:49,802
I've been looking for
her for a while, you know.

201
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:51,637
Let's find her. But wait.

202
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:52,930
Let's call security first.

203
00:07:53,014 --> 00:07:53,973
- We'll have him picked up.
- Oh, let's go, let's go.

204
00:07:54,056 --> 00:07:54,807
This lunatic.

205
00:07:54,891 --> 00:07:56,100
You-- you're nuts, huh.

206
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:57,685
- So, you're a thief, huh.
- You hit--

207
00:07:57,768 --> 00:07:59,520
- Come here.
- You even kept hitting me. Give me that.

208
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:02,398
- Come here. Come, come, come, come.
- You lunatic.

209
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:03,816
[music fades]

210
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:06,444
[ominous music playing]

211
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:14,827
- Oh, Sir Atoy.
- Hey--

212
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:15,995
[music continues]

213
00:08:16,078 --> 00:08:18,039
Sir-- ah, Sir-- Sir Atoy.

214
00:08:18,122 --> 00:08:19,373
What are you doing here?

215
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:20,958
Ah--

216
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:22,126
[music swells]

217
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:26,214
Geez, now she's gone.

218
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:27,965
You, what are you doing here?

219
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:29,383
Are you following someone?

220
00:08:29,467 --> 00:08:30,218
Following--

221
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:32,845
I'm following someone too.

222
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:35,890
The woman I suspect to
be the Washer came here.

223
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:39,143
Oh, did you see her?

224
00:08:39,227 --> 00:08:39,936
How would I see her?

225
00:08:40,019 --> 00:08:41,437
She disappeared, and then you arrived.

226
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:43,606
Oh. Sorry, okay.

227
00:08:43,689 --> 00:08:45,149
So, who are you peering at?

228
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:48,277
Samir, I saw him talking to someone.

229
00:08:48,361 --> 00:08:48,945
Samir?!

230
00:08:49,028 --> 00:08:49,529
Samir!

231
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:50,947
Really, Samir?!

232
00:08:51,030 --> 00:08:52,240
Oh, then I was right!

233
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:54,158
My prospect is here,

234
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:55,117
and Samir is here.

235
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:57,578
That means this is where they’ll meet up!

236
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:59,580
I knew it! I knew it!

237
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:00,748
We need to see her.

238
00:09:00,831 --> 00:09:02,375
- We really must!
- But, but…

239
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:04,418
But you need to let go of my clothes.

240
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:07,296
Ah-- right.

241
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:09,840
Jesabel: Sorry, Sir Atoy. Sorry.

242
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:11,467
I got carried away.

243
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:13,594
Ah, what does the…

244
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:15,721
Washer you're talking about look like?
What's the profile?

245
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:19,308
Ah, a mother who looks well-off.

246
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:24,564
Maybe her age is 45
to 55 years old, short hair.

247
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:26,148
[tense music playing]

248
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:27,942
Let's go.

249
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:30,820
Where?

250
00:09:30,903 --> 00:09:31,487
[music swells]

251
00:09:31,571 --> 00:09:33,364
Samir: ₱10 million donation.

252
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:38,703
One of many to come
until the plan is in place.

253
00:09:38,786 --> 00:09:41,747
Check? Samir, this has money trail.

254
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:45,293
It is from a shell corporation

255
00:09:45,376 --> 00:09:47,837
called Greenhop Alliance,

256
00:09:48,546 --> 00:09:50,548
but that is Obsidian's money.

257
00:09:50,631 --> 00:09:53,009
Once it hits the Harvest Aid book,

258
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:54,176
no one checks the source,

259
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,095
it's because that is charity.

260
00:09:57,096 --> 00:09:58,264
Understood.

261
00:09:58,973 --> 00:10:02,435
And from now on, we will stop doing

262
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:06,105
physical transaction because
The Master Cutter

263
00:10:06,772 --> 00:10:10,985
nearly interfered with
one of our transactions.

264
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:15,740
I know that he and the
Belladonna must be speaking.

265
00:10:16,699 --> 00:10:18,576
Who is this Master Cutter?

266
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:23,831
Just an old enemy of mine.

267
00:10:23,914 --> 00:10:25,416
[heavy music playing]

268
00:10:25,499 --> 00:10:28,878
He is after us, but he is only one man.

269
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:32,173
Of course,

270
00:10:32,923 --> 00:10:34,925
we shouldn't be complacent.

271
00:10:36,177 --> 00:10:37,845
I will handle him.

272
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:42,141
You handle washing the money. Okay?

273
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:43,768
[rousing music playing]

274
00:10:45,102 --> 00:10:47,605
[suspicious music playing]

275
00:10:50,232 --> 00:10:52,360
Sir Atoy, where could they have gone?

276
00:10:52,443 --> 00:10:53,569
Shh.

277
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:56,155
Huh? Do you want me
to start asking around here?

278
00:10:56,238 --> 00:10:57,657
Psst, shut up.

279
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:00,576
Why, Sir?

280
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:02,787
[music continues]

281
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:04,789
Samir was talking to a woman.

282
00:11:06,290 --> 00:11:08,918
There's a woman's shoe print here.

283
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:11,837
See. I was right!

284
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:13,506
This Emerson had better watch out.

285
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:15,049
Emerson: I'll beat him up.

286
00:11:15,132 --> 00:11:18,219
But there are many guests here who fit
the profile you described, you know.

287
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:20,012
Oh, when I see her,

288
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:21,931
I'll point her out to you right away.

289
00:11:22,014 --> 00:11:23,391
[music continues]

290
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:28,562
Wait a moment, because there's--

291
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:32,900
[heavy music playing]

292
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:46,163
Fringe detail…

293
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:47,998
[music continues]

294
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:49,417
Fringe detail.

295
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:52,169
[music continues]

296
00:11:53,796 --> 00:11:54,547
It smells nice, ah.

297
00:11:54,630 --> 00:11:55,881
[sniffs]

298
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:57,007
Smells like…

299
00:11:57,925 --> 00:11:59,718
citronella.

300
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,262
[music fades]

301
00:12:01,345 --> 00:12:02,930
Insect repellent?

302
00:12:03,013 --> 00:12:03,973
Here's your citronella spray.

303
00:12:04,056 --> 00:12:05,224
Thank you so much.

304
00:12:05,307 --> 00:12:06,934
- You're welcome.
- Anyway, I hope you both enjoy

305
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:07,726
this day.

306
00:12:08,561 --> 00:12:09,728
Audrey's boss?

307
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:12,815
[suspicious music playing]

308
00:12:14,525 --> 00:12:16,694
Could Audrey's boss be The Washer?

309
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:18,821
[music fades]

310
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:21,198
You now have control of money.

311
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:22,950
But be careful,

312
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:25,661
do not let that money get in trouble.

313
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:27,872
Samir, you know I can handle this.

314
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:30,416
[suspicious music playing]

315
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:35,004
Samir, someone broke into your room.

316
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:36,005
All your items were retrieved,

317
00:12:36,088 --> 00:12:37,423
and the thief was caught.

318
00:12:37,506 --> 00:12:39,592
But you need to come look.

319
00:12:39,675 --> 00:12:41,719
[speaks in Russian] I have to go.

320
00:12:41,802 --> 00:12:43,053
[music fades]

321
00:12:44,388 --> 00:12:45,306
[sighs]

322
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:48,017
Dolly: Shoes are killing me.

323
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:51,479
[tense music playing]

324
00:12:59,778 --> 00:13:02,198
[music fades]

325
00:13:02,281 --> 00:13:05,201
[phone ringing]

326
00:13:06,368 --> 00:13:07,369
Audrey, what is it?

327
00:13:07,453 --> 00:13:08,454
[smirks]

328
00:13:09,121 --> 00:13:10,414
Did you and Atoy check in already?

329
00:13:10,498 --> 00:13:13,042
Audrey on the phone: Yes,
but he suddenly disappeared.

330
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:16,420
Oka, what's going on with your friend?

331
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:18,923
I can't contact him yet.

332
00:13:19,006 --> 00:13:20,341
It's been a while, you know.

333
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:23,802
I don't understand whether
he wants to be with me or not.

334
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:24,845
[suspicious music playing]

335
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:27,264
Maybe he just went
to get something outside.

336
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:28,557
Audrey on the phone: No.

337
00:13:28,641 --> 00:13:32,520
I have a feeling Georgia
is the reason Atoy is missing.

338
00:13:33,812 --> 00:13:38,734
Oka, can you help me find out
where Georgia's cottage is?

339
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:39,777
Sure.

340
00:13:40,819 --> 00:13:41,779
I'll try.

341
00:13:42,821 --> 00:13:44,823
And then I'll message you once I have…

342
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:46,492
news.

343
00:13:46,575 --> 00:13:48,619
Audrey on the phone: Thank you.

344
00:13:48,702 --> 00:13:53,290
I just wanna make sure
I'm not being fooled by my husband.

345
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:56,085
Mmm-hmm. Anytime.

346
00:13:56,168 --> 00:13:58,170
[music continues]

347
00:13:59,672 --> 00:14:00,798
[phone blips]

348
00:14:01,507 --> 00:14:02,383
[music fades]

349
00:14:03,425 --> 00:14:05,386
Sir, thank you very much for your help.

350
00:14:05,469 --> 00:14:09,765
Well, that man's whole thing is
checking in to peddle women and steal.

351
00:14:09,848 --> 00:14:11,350
Hmm…

352
00:14:11,433 --> 00:14:13,769
Modus. So, it turns out
there was really no problem.

353
00:14:13,852 --> 00:14:15,020
No problem, brother.

354
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:16,021
Okay, okay!

355
00:14:16,730 --> 00:14:17,314
[smirks]

356
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:19,358
Imagine that, right?

357
00:14:19,441 --> 00:14:22,778
So that's why you saw him
approach Samir, because…

358
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:24,905
he was really planning to rob him.
[smirks]

359
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:27,157
Ugh. We caught a criminal.

360
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:30,119
And until now we still
haven't caught The Washer.

361
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:31,161
- The Washer.
- Good evening, sir.

362
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:34,748
The owner of the…
attaché case that you retrieved

363
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:37,293
from the intruder here at the
resort wants to thank you.

364
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:38,335
Okay, sure.

365
00:14:38,419 --> 00:14:40,129
- All right, have them come.
- It's fine, go ahead. Call them.

366
00:14:40,212 --> 00:14:40,838
Emerson: Who could that be?

367
00:14:40,921 --> 00:14:41,589
Sir!

368
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:45,509
- [indistinct chattering]
- Well, of course.

369
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:50,347
Gentlemen, I would just like
to say thank you for your service.

370
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:53,225
[coughing]
A little token of my appreciation.

371
00:14:53,309 --> 00:15:00,190
[coughing] [music continues]

372
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:01,734
Ah, ah, hmm…

373
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:02,860
No, no, no, no.

374
00:15:02,943 --> 00:15:04,320
We-- we are good samaritans.

375
00:15:04,403 --> 00:15:06,864
We don't like bad people,

376
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:07,698
ah, bad spirit.

377
00:15:07,781 --> 00:15:10,409
We don't like thieves, scammers and the--

378
00:15:10,492 --> 00:15:11,535
and the terrorists--

379
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:15,247
[muttering]

380
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:17,875
- [coughs]
- What is wrong with your friend?

381
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:18,959
Ah, him?

382
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:20,210
[coughing]

383
00:15:20,294 --> 00:15:21,545
Ah, virus! Virus!

384
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:22,588
- [coughing]
- Emerson: Virus.

385
00:15:22,671 --> 00:15:23,714
Virus! Yes!

386
00:15:23,797 --> 00:15:26,050
Well, thank you. I'm leaving, gentlemen.

387
00:15:26,133 --> 00:15:27,259
[clears throat]

388
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:28,260
Sir, excuse me.

389
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:29,929
Okay, go ahead.

390
00:15:30,012 --> 00:15:31,764
[soft rock music playing]

391
00:15:31,847 --> 00:15:32,890
[sighs]

392
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:35,184
There.

393
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:35,809
Mmm-hmm?

394
00:15:35,893 --> 00:15:37,645
Are we going to accept that money?

395
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:39,438
Who knows where that came from.

396
00:15:39,521 --> 00:15:41,482
Come on, come on.

397
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:42,232
Let's go!

398
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:43,233
Let's leave that.

399
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:44,652
[sighs]

400
00:15:44,735 --> 00:15:45,819
Samir.

401
00:15:47,321 --> 00:15:49,573
[music fades]

402
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:50,783
[pensive music playing]

403
00:15:50,866 --> 00:15:52,034
Ah, sis.

404
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:54,286
Excuse me.

405
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:55,663
[music continues]

406
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:56,580
Ah…

407
00:15:57,665 --> 00:16:01,335
Did you see which cottage
this couple is in,

408
00:16:02,586 --> 00:16:04,505
or did you see them?

409
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:07,049
Ma'am, they've already checked in.

410
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:09,927
But we can't say which room.

411
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:12,846
Oh, okay.

412
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:14,723
[music fades]

413
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:16,809
[suspicious music playing]

414
00:16:16,892 --> 00:16:19,937
Georgia: Most likely I'll see them
tomorrow at the breakfast buffet.

415
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:21,230
[music continues]

416
00:16:21,313 --> 00:16:22,481
[Georgia sighs]

417
00:16:22,564 --> 00:16:24,525
Ma'am, you look stressed out.

418
00:16:24,608 --> 00:16:27,361
Staff: Maybe you'd
like to avail of our massage.

419
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:32,783
Ah, sure. Anyway, I'm done for today.

420
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:35,494
What's your cottage and name?

421
00:16:35,577 --> 00:16:39,373
Ah, cottage 16, Georgia Santillan.

422
00:16:39,456 --> 00:16:41,667
Staff: Ah, okay.

423
00:16:41,750 --> 00:16:43,752
I'll send over our best massage therapist.

424
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:45,713
Just prepare and undress.

425
00:16:45,796 --> 00:16:47,423
Just lay flat on the bed.

426
00:16:47,506 --> 00:16:49,508
Okay. I will leave the door unlocked.

427
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:50,801
Thank you, Ma'am. Enjoy.

428
00:16:50,884 --> 00:16:51,885
Thank you.

429
00:16:57,057 --> 00:16:58,517
[music fades]

430
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:05,816
[suspicious music playing]

431
00:17:08,777 --> 00:17:13,407
[music continues]

432
00:17:44,271 --> 00:17:46,690
[device blipping]

433
00:17:46,774 --> 00:17:49,735
[suspicious music playing]

434
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:52,696
[music swells]

435
00:17:53,197 --> 00:17:55,783
Sir Atoy, that's my prospect.

436
00:17:55,866 --> 00:17:56,617
Are you sure?

437
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:57,618
I'm absolutely sure.

438
00:17:57,701 --> 00:18:00,579
Jesabel: That's the woman who took a
long time washing her hands at the faucet.

439
00:18:00,662 --> 00:18:02,122
[tense music playing]

440
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:03,499
Wh--

441
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:04,333
[music continues]

442
00:18:04,416 --> 00:18:05,793
I'll just do it myself.

443
00:18:05,876 --> 00:18:06,460
Atoy: Psst.

444
00:18:06,543 --> 00:18:08,128
Hey, hey! Hey!

445
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:10,380
You, woman! You don't look it, okay!

446
00:18:10,464 --> 00:18:12,132
But I know who you are!

447
00:18:12,966 --> 00:18:13,509
Huh?

448
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:14,802
What? Speak up!

449
00:18:14,885 --> 00:18:17,012
Excuse me? What are you saying?

450
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:20,599
Oh! Don't give me that excuse me, okay!

451
00:18:20,682 --> 00:18:21,767
I said…

452
00:18:22,351 --> 00:18:23,894
you're the bad person!

453
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:27,981
What? Speak up!

454
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:28,857
I know you!

455
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:30,359
- Atoy, are you with this girl?
- I'm telling you.

456
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:31,318
She is harassing me.

457
00:18:31,401 --> 00:18:33,028
- Ah, yes.
- Saying all sorts of things.

458
00:18:33,112 --> 00:18:34,154
I'm-- I'm sorry.

459
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:38,700
My friend didn't take her medicine
for the brain so she's hallucinating.

460
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:40,327
[soft rock music playing]

461
00:18:40,410 --> 00:18:41,120
Dolly: What?

462
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:42,538
Yeah. I'm-- I'm sorry.

463
00:18:42,621 --> 00:18:43,705
Psst.

464
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:45,874
Hah-hah-hay!

465
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:47,251
You, you too!

466
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:48,544
You too, huh!

467
00:18:48,627 --> 00:18:50,003
And now you're in violet!

468
00:18:50,087 --> 00:18:52,089
Jesabel: Did you think I don't know you?!

469
00:18:52,172 --> 00:18:54,424
I know your true character!

470
00:18:54,508 --> 00:18:55,717
- Oh my god, she's crazy.
- Jesabel: Ha! You think--

471
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:56,969
- Why is she even here?
- Sorry, it's--

472
00:18:57,052 --> 00:19:00,889
Atoy, restrain your companion
before she harms anyone.

473
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:02,474
- I have to be somewhere.
- Come on, come on.

474
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:03,892
- [bawls]
- Excuse me.

475
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:04,935
Come, come, come, come, come.

476
00:19:05,018 --> 00:19:06,728
- Let's go, let's go, let's go!
- There are no miracles!

477
00:19:06,812 --> 00:19:07,688
Let's go, let's go,
let's go, let's go, let's go.

478
00:19:07,771 --> 00:19:09,273
Jesabel: God's mercy is up to Him!

479
00:19:09,356 --> 00:19:10,065
Yes, yes, yes.

480
00:19:10,149 --> 00:19:10,899
All right, I feel bad for her too.

481
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:13,152
[suspicious music playing]

482
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:15,070
You'd better get ready, Atoy.

483
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:18,448
Once I find out you're with that Georgia.

484
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:20,868
[music continues]

485
00:19:22,494 --> 00:19:23,620
[phone blips]

486
00:19:23,704 --> 00:19:25,873
[music continues]

487
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:41,054
She's my wife's boss.

488
00:19:41,638 --> 00:19:42,472
Honestly,

489
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:44,766
I'm not sure if she's The Washer.

490
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:47,853
Jesabel, it seems like the
approach you took was wrong.

491
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:49,396
You shouldn't have
rushed at her like that,

492
00:19:49,479 --> 00:19:50,814
what you did was dangerous.

493
00:19:50,898 --> 00:19:52,482
Sorry, Master.

494
00:19:52,983 --> 00:19:56,069
Well, why did you say that…

495
00:19:56,153 --> 00:19:57,905
you're not sure about her?

496
00:19:58,864 --> 00:20:04,995
Because we're looking for a person
in heels with pink fringe details.

497
00:20:05,078 --> 00:20:05,913
Okay?

498
00:20:06,496 --> 00:20:07,581
But when I saw Ms. Dolly earlier,

499
00:20:07,664 --> 00:20:09,666
she wasn't wearing heels, she was in…

500
00:20:10,292 --> 00:20:13,128
flats. But we don't know
if maybe she changed.

501
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:13,879
Jesabel: Right?

502
00:20:13,962 --> 00:20:17,716
And besides, many women here have
the same kind of shoes.

503
00:20:18,383 --> 00:20:20,135
And the citronella.

504
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:20,928
Jesabel: That's it.

505
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:21,720
That citronella, can be--

506
00:20:21,803 --> 00:20:23,430
Ah, how can you say citro--

507
00:20:23,513 --> 00:20:25,307
So many people have citronella.

508
00:20:25,390 --> 00:20:27,559
My wife even has
a citronella spray, you know.

509
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:28,769
Ah…

510
00:20:29,353 --> 00:20:32,272
Sir, listen. Just hear me out.

511
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:37,653
She's the one the Russian man
approached at the faucet.

512
00:20:37,736 --> 00:20:39,238
Then she washed her hands, you know.

513
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:42,074
- Oh? That's it?
- That's it.

514
00:20:42,157 --> 00:20:43,242
- Jesabel: Yes.
- Ah, so that means,

515
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:45,035
just because a Russian-speaking

516
00:20:45,118 --> 00:20:45,661
person approached her,

517
00:20:45,744 --> 00:20:46,912
she's The Washer?

518
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:49,456
Jesabel, as Emerson said,

519
00:20:49,539 --> 00:20:51,208
there are many Russians here.

520
00:20:51,875 --> 00:20:53,001
Look, the groom is Russian.

521
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:55,295
Of course, his guests are Russian.

522
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:57,547
[suspicious music playing]

523
00:20:57,631 --> 00:20:58,632
Look.

524
00:20:59,633 --> 00:21:03,053
Clues are just clues. Okay?

525
00:21:03,136 --> 00:21:05,514
We can't conclude anything yet,

526
00:21:05,597 --> 00:21:07,057
because we still need to analyze,

527
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:09,601
we need to get more information.

528
00:21:11,228 --> 00:21:12,187
Okay?

529
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:14,815
[somber music playing]

530
00:21:15,857 --> 00:21:17,901
I need to go back to my wife now.

531
00:21:19,069 --> 00:21:20,654
Ah, she's looking for me.

532
00:21:20,737 --> 00:21:23,740
Ah, maybe you could buy me
some juice or anything…

533
00:21:24,408 --> 00:21:25,033
I can bring,

534
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:27,953
so she'll know I just bought something.

535
00:21:28,036 --> 00:21:29,079
[pensive music playing]

536
00:21:29,162 --> 00:21:30,706
Sorry, Master.

537
00:21:30,789 --> 00:21:31,707
Okay.

538
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:33,959
[music continues]

539
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:42,634
Samir…

540
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:44,386
we're on the way.

541
00:21:44,469 --> 00:21:46,054
[music swells]

542
00:21:48,223 --> 00:21:51,059
[ominous music playing]

543
00:21:58,775 --> 00:21:59,735
That is Atoy.

544
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:01,778
Is it not?

545
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:03,655
Yes.

546
00:22:03,739 --> 00:22:05,365
The one who killed
your half-brother, Artem.

547
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:07,326
[tense music playing]

548
00:22:07,409 --> 00:22:08,243
Okay.

549
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:10,454
Message to Samir.

550
00:22:10,537 --> 00:22:11,663
Tell him not to wait.

551
00:22:12,456 --> 00:22:14,082
We will see him later.

552
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:17,544
[music swells]

553
00:22:17,627 --> 00:22:19,629
[suspenseful music playing]

554
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:34,686
[bullets whizzing]

555
00:22:35,562 --> 00:22:37,355
Get him.

556
00:22:37,439 --> 00:22:41,735
[tense music playing]

557
00:22:42,986 --> 00:22:46,406
[bullets whizzes]

558
00:22:47,074 --> 00:22:50,744
[bullets whizzing]

559
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:53,246
- Sir, your juice.
- Get out of here.

560
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:55,207
Go find Paldo and the others.

561
00:22:55,290 --> 00:22:58,251
Okay. Ah-- ah, I'll take this, okay?

562
00:22:58,335 --> 00:22:58,919
[music swells]

563
00:22:59,002 --> 00:23:00,921
[bullets whizzing]

564
00:23:01,004 --> 00:23:06,093
[rousing music playing]

565
00:23:10,472 --> 00:23:14,017
[electronic blipping]

566
00:23:14,101 --> 00:23:16,520
[intense music playing]

567
00:23:16,603 --> 00:23:18,313
Uno, please check on Master.

568
00:23:18,396 --> 00:23:20,899
Because I know there's
World War 3 at their house.

569
00:23:20,982 --> 00:23:22,609
Let's not meddle in…

570
00:23:22,692 --> 00:23:24,444
the couple's fight.

571
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:25,237
At the end of the day,

572
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:27,572
they'll realize they're family,

573
00:23:27,656 --> 00:23:28,865
and they love each other.

574
00:23:28,949 --> 00:23:30,158
Oka, be honest with me.

575
00:23:30,242 --> 00:23:30,909
Oh?

576
00:23:30,992 --> 00:23:33,453
You really want Audrey and
Atoy to break up, don't you?

577
00:23:33,537 --> 00:23:35,956
Because you plan to take Audrey away.

578
00:23:36,039 --> 00:23:37,374
Emerson: I can see right through you.

579
00:23:37,457 --> 00:23:38,708
[theme music playing]

580
00:23:38,792 --> 00:23:40,377
If only there were medicine

581
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:45,757
to make a person believe
that we're not doing anything wrong?

582
00:23:46,466 --> 00:23:47,926
I'd buy it.

583
00:23:48,885 --> 00:23:50,679
But, why?

584
00:23:50,762 --> 00:23:52,681
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

585
00:23:52,764 --> 00:23:56,143
Rachel C. Arias Script
Producer/Closed Caption Transcriptionist

586
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:57,936
(♪ Fix this ♪)
